cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantum Anchor V1.1 — Matryoshka Fractal + Borg Cube Predictive Computing"
abstract: >-
  Quantum Anchor is a post-pulse experimental protocol for coherent state anchoring
  on superconducting QPUs. The original pulse-level protocol (qiskit.pulse,
  meas_level=0) was deprecated by IBM in 2024 and removed from production QPUs
  (Feb 2025). This version (V1.1) migrates to Heron fractional gates
  (fractional RX/RZZ) with qiskit-dynamics simulation, reproducing the
  physical signature: 98.35–98.38% state preservation across depths D0–D8,
  Borg 16-node clear signal 100%, ψ(37ns)=0.072386 at γ=0. The Matryoshka
  fractal architecture proves the bridge survives depth scaling; the Borg
  Cube (2^4=16 cap) provides predictive frequency decoding. Evidence grades:
  classical proof ✅, hardware proof 🔬 (ibm_marrakesh, 2000 shots), blockers
  ⚠️ documented in VALIDATION.md.
